  "answer": "Citation complaints dropped sharply from Q1 to Q2. In Q1 2026, there was a sharp increase in citation-error tickets, with an audit of 210 accuracy-related tickets showing categories such as incorrect file links, missing page numbers, empty citations, and broken links [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. Monthly citation accuracy tickets fell from 72 in January, 79 in February, and 88 in March to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June after the April product release [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The April fixes significantly reduced citation-related complaints [NL-016#NL-016-S04]. However, the remaining citation tickets in May and June were almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs, where TutorChat struggles to establish citation anchors [NL-011#NL-011-S05].\n\nThe planned product work that directly addresses the remaining scanned-document problem is the **Advanced OCR Pipeline**, scheduled for release/pilot in August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. This pipeline is designed to automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned, image-only files, enabling page-specific citations instead of missing links or citations pointing to page 1 of a large document [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
